 think um  what happened at first was everybody was  just so afraid like right we were  getting those photos from china and some  videos and stuff like that it was like  this thing is coming to america you know  when is it gonna pop up there was cases  and then you hear that a player in the  nba has it and and you know had spread  it to his teammates and so because of  the way that it was it was portrayed in  the media it was just such a fearful  time i feel like everybody was walking  on eggshells um thinking about when when  they were going to get it and so once  the nba had shut down we had time to  kind of just you know i think we went on  a quarantine really i think right around  that time um at least florida had like a  curfew it wasn't a complete um you know  lockdown but we had a curfew that you  had to be in your house and it was just  a weird time but um you know social  media wasn't a big help because of all  the things that we're spreading and  going around and so i just tried my best  to kind of take a step back and just  watch everything um there was there was  an early  hesitation with me because of the way  that things were being portrayed um it  seemed like everything was so forced and  and and and made to be fearful for  everyone to kind of be running around  like chickens with their head cuts off  so i kind of just took a step back and  said let me watch and then we get to the  bubble and then after that we get to  okay now there's a vaccine on the scene  and that's that's the that's that's that  we get a little later if you're looking  for more honest and thoughtful  conversations about politics instead of  non-stop yelling check out our politics  playlist and if you want to watch full  interviews on a variety of topics watch  our full episode playlist all right over  here and to get notified of all future  videos be sure to subscribe and click  the notification bell

